  "conventions": {
    "frame_size": "<integer>",
    "statistics": "median and interquartile range over active frames, quantiles by linear interpolation at q (n - 1) between the sorted values; a frame is active when its RMS lies within 40 dB of the loudest frame",
    "spectral": "magnitude weights for shape, power for band shares; periodic Hann frames of frame_size samples, hop frame_size / 4, centred and zero-padded; frame_size is 8192 when the note list has a median f0 below 100 Hz, else 4096, and 4096 without a note list",
    "bpm": "the tempo of the beat grid and of every later step: bpm_refined when its confidence is high, else bpm_given",
    "bpm_given": "given by --bpm",
    "bpm_refined": "onset strength: the rise of each third-octave band power from 30 Hz, compressed as ln(1 + P / knee) with the knee 60 dB below full scale, against the frame 10 ms earlier, in 46.4 ms Hann frames on a 1 ms hop, low-passed at 20 Hz, less its 100 ms mean, below 10 % of its largest rise set to 0; each tempo t with |given / t - 1| at most 3 % (2.91 % below to 3.09 % above the given one), in 0.01 BPM steps, scores the unbiased autocorrelation summed at 1 to 32 beats; the refined tempo is used when its score is at least 1.5 times the median score (tempo_peak) and either 0.4 of the lag count times the zero-lag autocorrelation (beat_periodicity), or 0.75 of that on every second or fourth beat lag alone (sparse_periodicity) with at most 0.8 peaks of the onset strength per beat (onsets_per_beat), and at least 0.9 of the energy of the rise before its low-pass lies within 25 ms of its peaks, each the largest within 30 ms (onset_sharpness); both shares stop at 1; cycles_in_span counts the whole beats of the stem",
    "duration_s": "decoded frames over the sample rate",
    "sample_rate_hz": "the native rate of the file; no resampling",
    "band_edge_hz": "long-term power spectrum of the mid over the active frames that lie wholly inside the stem, median-smoothed over one semitone on each side; where the smoothed level falls at least 25 dB over one semitone above 2 kHz and the median level of the octave below lies within 20 dB of the level where the fall starts, the edge is the half-depth point of the steepest such fall; otherwise the noise floor is the lowest level above 1 kHz and the edge is the highest bin at least 30 dB above it, at low confidence, or the Nyquist frequency when no bin above 1 kHz is",
    "hard_limited": "true when runs of at least 1 ms of samples within 1e-5 of the channel peak, each with its neighbours on both sides at least half the peak on the same side, cover at least 0.1 % of a channel",
    "peak_dbfs": "peak and RMS of the mono mix over the whole stem in dB relative to full scale 1.0; a full-scale sine reads -3.01 dB RMS; crest is peak minus RMS",
    "rms_dbfs": "peak and RMS of the mono mix over the whole stem in dB relative to full scale 1.0; a full-scale sine reads -3.01 dB RMS; crest is peak minus RMS",
    "crest_db": "peak and RMS of the mono mix over the whole stem in dB relative to full scale 1.0; a full-scale sine reads -3.01 dB RMS; crest is peak minus RMS",
    "centroid_hz": "magnitude weights |X_k| divided by the window sum, periodic Hann frames, statistics over active frames as median and interquartile range",
    "centroid_over_f0": "the centroid of each active frame over the median f0 of the note list, MIDI pitch to hertz with A4 = 440 Hz; null without a note list",
    "spread_hz": "magnitude weights |X_k| divided by the window sum, periodic Hann frames, statistics over active frames as median and interquartile range",
    "rolloff85_hz": "magnitude weights |X_k| divided by the window sum, periodic Hann frames, statistics over active frames as median and interquartile range",
    "rolloff95_hz": "magnitude weights |X_k| divided by the window sum, periodic Hann frames, statistics over active frames as median and interquartile range",
    "flatness": "geometric over arithmetic mean of the magnitude, floored at 1e-5 after the window-sum scale, bins from 100 Hz to 10 kHz",
    "band_share": "power |X_k|^2 summed over active frames per band, divided by the power in the bands reported; bands start at 20, 60, 250, 1000, 4000 and 10000 Hz and end at the next start or 20 kHz; a band that starts at or above the Nyquist frequency is left out, and one that crosses it ends there",
    "stereo": "rho: Pearson correlation at zero lag; sm_db: 20 log10(rms(S) / rms(M)) with M = (L + R) / 2 and S = (L - R) / 2; per band from the 8192-point Hann STFT over bins inside the band, DC excluded; ipd_deg: abs(angle(L conj R)) at the largest cross-spectrum bin within 2 bins of h f0, h = 1..20 inside the band, weighted by |L conj R|, then the mean over active frames, whose RMS over both channels, sqrt((rms_L^2 + rms_R^2) / 2), lies within 40 dB of the loudest; bands: sub below 120 Hz, low_mid 120 Hz to 1 kHz, high above 1 kHz",
    "confidence": "level, reasons and spread of each estimate; the spread of a statistic is its interquartile range and that of the band edge one bin width, in the unit of the value; estimate false means no value, with the reasons why",
    "pitch": "the pitch layer of a monophonic line, read from the f0 track, the note list and the sub-band line; values is null when the line plays chords or has no notes; every time is audio time from the start of the stem",
    "glides": "pitch in cents of the voiced f0 frames; a stable pitch is a span of 50 ms or more within 30 cents of its running mean whose least-squares slope stays at 86 cents per second or less; a glide joins two stable pitches 100 cents or more apart that match notes of different pitch within 50 cents, where the slope of the 5-frame moving average stays at 86 cents per second or more, in the direction of the motion, over 35 ms or more; s(x) = 1 - (1 - x)^p is fitted between the two stable pitches by least squares over the motion and 50 ms of each; start_s is the fitted start less the track's lag of a quarter frame, 23.2 ms, less half a period; time_s is the full 0 to 100 % time; from_silence marks a glide into the first stable pitch of a voiced run whose sound starts, the full-band RMS rising 20 dB, up to 100 ms before it, when that stable pitch has a median level within 40 dB of the loudest frame and the smoothed pitch does not swing back 50 % of the lead within half a period of 3 Hz after it, unless the run's next stable pitch lies 100 cents or more away and matches another note, the nearest match counting, and the pitch, once past half the way to it, stays there up to that stable pitch and to the window's end, and the fit also finds its start pitch; a voiced run that starts within 100 ms of the one before joins it when the full-band RMS does not rise 6 dB in the gap, its 10 ms RMS stays within 20 dB of the 20 ms before or after the gap and within 40 dB of the loudest frame of the stem, and the pitch keeps moving after the gap the way it jumped, at 30 cents per millisecond or slower; two stable pitches with a bridged gap between them whose jump goes against the interval by 20 cents or more, or carries more than 60 % of it, join no glide; motion of 35 to 90 ms over the fitted time, or over the detected span when the fit fails, counts as too short; a fit of 90 ms or more with p within 5 % of 0.2, with p within 5 % of 5 and an RMS residual above 20 cents, a detected span under 90 ms or over 2.5 times the fitted time, or a start from silence, or with an RMS residual above 40 cents, is no glide; a glide with p within 5 % of 5 reads at low confidence with the reason curve_bound, and so does one whose detected span lasts under 90 ms",
    "drops": "f(t) = f_end + df exp(-t / tau) fitted by least squares to the sub-band line from 7 ms to 400 ms after the onset, or to the end of the note; tau by a log grid and golden-section search from 3.04 ms, where exp(-7 ms / tau) = 0.1, to 1 s, f_end and df linear for each tau; a fit with tau under 10 ms, or after a strike whose full-band RMS rises 20 dB, is fitted again on the line with its high-pass at 10 Hz, and the refit counts; df_st = 12 log2((f_end + df) / f_end); onset_s is the first sample after the lowest point of the onset search where the 20 to 200 Hz envelope, averaged over a centred 10 ms, reaches half the peak that follows; a strike whose full-band RMS over the 20 ms after the onset lies more than 40 dB below the loudest 25 ms frame of the stem, or whose 20 to 200 Hz RMS over those 20 ms lies more than 18 dB below the loudest 25 ms frame of that band, is no candidate; a drop with tau under 10 ms needs an envelope that takes 30 ms or less from 10 to 90 % of its peak; a drop with tau under 10 ms, one that starts at 200 Hz or above, or one whose envelope takes over 30 ms from 10 to 90 % of its peak needs the full-band RMS over the 20 ms after the onset 6 dB or more above the 20 ms that end 25 ms before it; residual is the RMS of the fit's error, averaged over half a period of f_end when tau is 10 ms or more and over a full period when tau spans 1.5 periods or more, over the fitted fall from 7 ms on, df exp(-7 ms / tau); a drop counts when df_st is above 2 and at most 36, that fall is above 2 semitones too, tau is above the bound of the search, residual is below 0.15, and f_end lies within 100 cents of a note that starts 150 ms or less before the onset and sounds at some point from 5 tau after the onset, or from the end of the fit span if that comes first, to the end of the fit span; a fit after a 6 dB strike that is no drop is fitted again on the note line, whose low-pass sits at 1.5 times the note's pitch, when that lies under 200 Hz, with its span ending one period of the note before the note line's frequency first falls to 0 Hz, and the refit counts with tau of 10 ms or more and an RMS envelope over its fall, from 7 ms to 5 tau, at most 6 dB below the line the first fit read; a search that starts where the previous note's search ended, before the drop read last has settled, 5 tau after its onset, finds that strike again when its 20 to 200 Hz envelope, averaged over a centred 2 periods of the note, is lowest at its first sample",
    "sub_band_line": "fourth-order Butterworth high-pass at 20 Hz and low-pass at 200 Hz, each forward and backward; the frequency of the analytic signal between consecutive samples, arg(z[n+1] conj(z[n])) fs / 2 pi; a centred median of round(1.4 ms fs) samples, made odd, shortened at the ends; the refit of a drop uses a high-pass at 10 Hz",
    "vibrato": "the voiced f0 frames of a steady span, a voiced run of the track split where two stable pitches lie 150 cents or more apart, without 50 ms at each end, without the frames where a glide's fitted curve lies more than 10 cents from both its pitches and without a drop: the span before it ends 50 ms before its onset, and the span after starts once it has settled, five time constants and at least 100 ms after the onset; in cents; start_s and end_s are its first and last frame in audio time; a least-squares line and sine fitted together, at the rate whose sine explains the most power beyond the line, searched from 1 Hz or 1.5 cycles over the span up to 20 Hz in 0.01 Hz steps and refined by golden-section search; extent_raw_ct is that sine's amplitude, half the peak-to-peak swing; extent_ct is extent_raw_ct times extent_factor, which undoes the smoothing of the f0 track at that rate; a vibrato counts at 2.97 to 12.12 Hz, 3 to 12 Hz with 1 % slack, with extent_ct of 10 or more and a share, the power the sine explains beyond the line, the line's residual less that of the line and sine together, over the power left after the line alone, of 0.5 or more, over 2.5 cycles or more",
    "envelope": "each note is read on a 1 ms hop from 30 ms before its onset in the note list to its end; the amp proxy is the note's lowest harmonic among the first three that lies 30 Hz or more from every harmonic of the notes sounding with it: for a note that overlaps no other, a sliding DFT over one period of the fundamental, else the zero-phase band magnitude, low-passed at half the distance to the nearest foreign or own neighbouring harmonic, 12 to 40 Hz; levels are dB from the note's peak of the amp proxy, read no lower than -60 dB; attack_s is 1.25 times the 10 to 90 % rise of the linear amplitude to the attack's top, the full 0 to 100 % time of a linear ramp, read on the centred RMS over one period of the fundamental, or the fewest whole periods that span 2 ms, for a note that overlaps no other, else on the amp proxy; the top is the first frame from the onset that the level exceeds by less than 1 dB over as long again as it took to rise to it from under 10 % of it, and at least over the shortest rise the track can tell, the upper bound's figure below, and the shares are of the highest frame over that span; the attack is an upper bound when the rise is shorter than 1.5 RMS windows, or on the amp proxy shorter than 0.98 over its low-pass cutoff, twice its rise for an instant step; hold_s is the time from the first frame within 1 dB of the peak to the start of the decay, 0 when under 10 ms; decay_s is the time between the first frames after the peak, linear between frames, at which the level falls through 10 % and 90 % of the sustain level in dB, the first at least 0.5 dB down, divided by the gap between the two shares, and the decay starts the first share of it before the first; sustain_db is the median of the last 30 % of the held part, from the first frame within 1 dB of the peak to the note-off knee, or to 25 ms before the note's end without one; decay and sustain are null when a note with a knee holds for less than the attack, the hold and three decay times, and a note without one sustains at its end level; fit_residual_db is the median over the pool of the RMS in dB of each held part against 0 dB over the hold, a fall linear in dB to the sustain level over the decay, then the sustain level; ripple_db is the median, over the pooled notes whose sustain is observable, of the 90th minus the 10th percentile of the sustain window after its line; each statistic is the median and interquartile range over the pooled notes: of the notes whose peak lies less than 12 dB below the peak of every note they overlap, those whose length to the knee, or to the end without one, lies within a factor of 2 of their median length and whose pitch lies within 12 semitones of their median pitch; a value over fewer than 3 notes, with an interquartile range above half its median, or with a median of 0 under an interquartile range above 0, has low confidence; attack_is_upper_bound is set when more than half the pooled attacks are upper bounds; a note whose amp proxy peaks at -120 dB or lower is skipped as silent",
    "note_off": "the note-off knee is read on the linear amplitude of the amp proxy, from the first frame within 1 dB of the peak to 25 ms before the note's end; at each split a line over up to 100 ms before it and one over up to 200 ms after it, stopping where the level falls under 2 % of the mean before it, fit against one line over both; a split counts when the right line is steeper by half the mean before it per second, falls by half that mean over its side, and the two lines leave at most half the squared error of one; splits that count in a row form a corner, and the split with the largest gain in the last corner wins; the knee is where the left line crosses a line over the first 10 ms after the split, or the split itself when that crossing lies outside the two lines; null when no split counts, as for a pluck that decays at one rate; note_off_offset_s is the note's end in the note list minus its knee, over the pooled notes with a knee",
    "level_spread_db": "the 90th minus the 10th percentile of the peak dB of the amp proxy over the pooled notes, quantiles by linear interpolation; always low confidence, a rule no stem has tested; null under 3 pooled notes",
    "pump": "the full-band centred RMS in dB over two periods of the lowest note on a 1 ms hop, cut into beats of the used tempo from 0 s; a beat counts when the held part of one note covers it, from 50 ms or more before it, the held part running from the note's onset to its knee, or to 25 ms before its end without one; each counted beat is binned into 64 phase bins and taken relative to the 90th percentile of its bins, and the curve is the median over the beats; pump_depth_db is minus the curve's minimum; pump_recovery_s is the time from the minimum until the curve comes back within 1.5 dB, going on over the beat's wrap, null when it does not within one beat; pump_tau_ms is pump_recovery_s over ln(pump_depth_db / 1.5), in milliseconds, null unless the pump locks to the beat; pump_locked_to is note when the beats with a note onset inside, from 50 ms before the beat, dip 3 dB or more and the others under 1.5 dB, each group of 2 beats or more; else free when the level swings 1 dB or more at a rate of 0.5 to 20 Hz that lies 50 cents or more from every note division; else beat when the curve dips 3 dB or more in one run of bins half its depth down, falls into its dip within 8 bins, reading on into the beat before, the odd and the even beats' own median curves do the same to half its depth at its dip, and half the beats fall by half its depth from their highest bin over the 8 bins before the 3 bins either side of the dip to their lowest within those; else none; the read at the period up to about 2.7 % from the tempo's whose counted beats fold onto the deepest mean curve replaces this read if that reads beat and this one reads note or none, reads beat 1.5 dB or more shallower without giving up the strip, or reads free on a line within 60 cents of a division under a curve that falls faster than it recovers and takes 3 bins and half the level window from half its depth back to a quarter; the curve is stripped from the tracks of a note only when it locks to the beat over 8 counted beats or more and the median fall of the beats over the note reaches half the curve's depth, the beats counted again over each note to 25 ms before its end when the held parts give fewer or no pump; null with fewer than 4 counted beats"
  }
}
